# myflow — start → do → finish

When running `/myflow-*` commands, follow this **fixed three-state pipeline**:

```text
/myflow-start  → STARTED      you: read the proposal artifact
/myflow-do     → IN_PROGRESS  you: review the staged diff and run the apps
/myflow-finish → FINISHED     terminal (second run — it integrates first)
```

Each command ends in the state named after it. The human gate is a property of the state, not a
separate step — which is why no command exists whose only job is to record that a review
happened. `/myflow-do` produces both the staged diff and the manual test guide, so reviewing and
testing are one gate. Every command is re-entrant, and a fix never moves the state.

`/myflow-finish` runs **twice**: once to integrate the branch (open a PR by default, merge, or
leave it to you), and again once the branch is merged to sync, archive, push and remove the
worktrees.

## Load the pipeline before acting

This rule is always on, in every session, so it carries **only the trigger above** — not the
pipeline itself. The pipeline is one file, loaded on demand:

**States** and **State transitions** (`skills/myflow-contracts/pipeline.md`) — **load that file
first**, before any other step of any `/myflow-*` command. It is canonical for the state
definitions, the command→state transition table, the wrong-state handoff, git boundaries, the
handoff output shape, and the finish contract.

Never act on a remembered version of any of that. A command that skips the load is running on a
stale copy of the state machine — the failure this split exists to prevent.

Seven narrower contracts sit beside it; load the one a step actually needs, not the directory:

| Contract | Load it before |
|----------|----------------|
| **State file** (`skills/myflow-contracts/state-file.md`) | reading or writing a change's state file |
| **State self-heal** (`skills/myflow-contracts/state-self-heal.md`) | validating or correcting a state file |
| **Project configuration** (`skills/myflow-contracts/project-configuration.md`) | resolving `.myflow/project.md` |
| **Jira integration** (`skills/myflow-contracts/jira-integration.md`) | any Jira-related step |
| **Plan provenance** (`skills/myflow-contracts/plan-provenance.md`) | writing or checking a plan's provenance tags |
| **The build-green tag** (`skills/myflow-contracts/build-green.md`) | writing or checking a task's build tag |
| **Workspace isolation** (`skills/myflow-contracts/workspace-isolation.md`) | resolving a worktree's own database, cache index, bucket or ports |

These files are installed alongside the skills in every harness — `~/.claude/skills/`,
`~/.cursor/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` — so the paths above resolve wherever this rule is read.
